      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We know GoFundMe acts as a volunteer-driven non-profit organization, and volunteers who contributed $10 or more felt it was going towards fighting Covid-19 cases in India and Argentina, so we will take 50 times the divisibe amount, so:\n\n$10\\times 1=10$\n$10\\times 2=20$\n$10\\times 3=30$\n$10\\times 4=40$\n$10\\times 5=50$ \nAfter the request was made we double the deadline by 1 week giving the money a new deadline of March 15, 2021. So after 1 week, the funds were converted into a cheque of $150$, valid for March 15, 2021. We can ignore the total and try to find the amount itself by slashing the total amount of $150$. If 150 is divided by original monthly payments and we go step by step by eliminating the amount, then we see that if $m$ was 30, we found the amount to be 117 of May 15 because \n\n$30\\times 117=3510$\n$3510\\div 20=175.5$\nIf we look at $\\boxed{17555}$ and set that as the first set of months we can see that it's divisible by 6 as $6 \\times 259 = 1554$, so if that was 150 years we would be missing 175 years, or 5 years can be deducted from the whole 150 years. So then that means the amount we want to be equals $17555 - 5$. That means the amount would be $\\boxed{17550}$.",
